# Git: push only when the user says so

**Default:** You may **`git add`** and **`git commit`** when saving work to version control.

**Push:** Run **`git push`** (or any remote-updating equivalent) **only if the user explicitly tells you to push in that same message** — e.g. “commit and push”, “push to GitHub”, “push origin main”, “run git push”. If they only say “commit” or do not mention push, **do not push**.

**Do not** push because you assume the work is “done”, because CI passed, or to “help” sync the remote — wait for an explicit push instruction.

**Other remotes:** Same rule for `gh pr create` / force-push / etc.: only when the user clearly asks in that turn.

If the user later says “always push after commit” or similar, follow that updated instruction for subsequent turns.
